==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|skiljanan|to separate, limit|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|(s)kalǝ-||(s)kelǝ-|to split, cut|lang=non}}. Compare {{etyl|xcl|-}} {{term|ցելում||tr=cʿelum|lang=xcl}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{term|scylian|lang=ang}}, {{term|scielian||to divide, separate|lang=ang}}. More at {{l|en|skill}}.

===Verb===
{{head|non|verb}}

# to [[part]], [[divide]], [[separate]]
# to [[break off]], [[break up]]
# to part company, take leave
# to [[distinguish]], [[discern]]
# to [[understand]], [[find out]]
# to [[decide]], [[settle]]
# to set apart, reserve for one

===References===
* {{R:non:Zoega}}
